#: ../../manual/editors/3dview/controls/pivot_point/3d_cursor.rst:19
msgid "The image below shows the difference between rotating an object around the 3D Cursor (left) and rotating it around the :doc:`Median Point </editors/3dview/controls/pivot_point/median_point>` (right)."
msgstr "Bilden nedan visar skillnaden mellan att rotera ett objekt runt 3D-markören (vänster) och att rotera det runt :doc:`Median Point </editors/3dview/controls/pivot_point/median_point>` (höger)."

#: ../../manual/editors/3dview/controls/pivot_point/3d_cursor.rst:26
msgid "Rotation around the 3D Cursor compared to the Median Point."
msgstr "Rotation runt 3D-markören jämfört med medianpunkten."

#: ../../manual/editors/3dview/controls/pivot_point/active_element.rst:4
#: ../../manual/modeling/metas/properties.rst:77
msgid "Active Element"
msgstr "Aktivt element"

#: ../../manual/editors/3dview/controls/pivot_point/active_element.rst:9
msgid ":menuselection:`Header --> Transform Pivot Point --> Active Element` (:bl-icon:`pivot_active`)"
msgstr ":menuselection:`Huvud --> Transform Pivot Point --> Aktivt Element` (:bl-icon:`pivot_active`)"

#: ../../manual/editors/3dview/controls/pivot_point/active_element.rst:12
msgid "Places the pivot point at the active element, which is the element that was selected most recently."
msgstr "Placerar pivotpunkten vid det aktiva elementet, vilket är det element som valdes senast."

#: ../../manual/editors/3dview/controls/pivot_point/active_element.rst:16
#: ../../manual/editors/3dview/controls/pivot_point/bounding_box_center.rst:17
#: ../../manual/editors/3dview/controls/pivot_point/individual_origins.rst:16
#: ../../manual/editors/3dview/controls/pivot_point/median_point.rst:16
msgid "In Object Mode"
msgstr "I objektläge"

#: ../../manual/editors/3dview/controls/pivot_point/active_element.rst:18
msgid "When in Object Mode, rotation and scaling happen around the origin of the active object, which is the element with a lighter outline than the others."
msgstr "I objektläget sker rotation och skalning runt det aktiva objektets ursprung, vilket är det element som har en ljusare kontur än de andra."

#: ../../manual/editors/3dview/controls/pivot_point/active_element.rst:22
msgid "The effect of the pivot point is shown in the image below, where the active object (the cube) remains in the same location while the others move."
msgstr "Effekten av pivotpunkten visas i bilden nedan, där det aktiva objektet (kuben) ligger kvar på samma plats medan de andra rör sig."

#: ../../manual/editors/3dview/controls/pivot_point/active_element.rst:28
msgid "Starting point, rotation, and scaling."
msgstr "Startpunkt, rotation och skalning."

#: ../../manual/editors/3dview/controls/pivot_point/active_element.rst:32
#: ../../manual/editors/3dview/controls/pivot_point/bounding_box_center.rst:47
#: ../../manual/editors/3dview/controls/pivot_point/individual_origins.rst:42
#: ../../manual/editors/3dview/controls/pivot_point/median_point.rst:34
msgid "In Edit Mode"
msgstr "I redigeringsläge"

#: ../../manual/editors/3dview/controls/pivot_point/active_element.rst:34
msgid "When in Edit Mode, rotation and scaling happen around the centerpoint of the active element, which is the element with a white outline. That centerpoint remains in the same location while everything else is transformed around it."
msgstr "I redigeringsläget sker rotation och skalning runt det aktiva elementets mittpunkt, som är det element som har en vit kontur. Denna mittpunkt förblir på samma plats medan allt annat transformeras runt den."

#: ../../manual/editors/3dview/controls/pivot_point/active_element.rst:39
msgid "The image below illustrates rotation around the active vertex, edge, and face. Each time, the active element rotates in place, while the others \"orbit\" around it. In the case of vertices, the active vertex is not changed at all, as a vertex on its own is just a point that has no concept of rotation."
msgstr "Bilden nedan illustrerar rotationen runt den aktiva vertexen, kanten och ytan. Varje gång roterar det aktiva elementet på plats, medan de andra \"kretsar\" runt det. När det gäller vertex ändras inte den aktiva vertexen alls, eftersom en vertex i sig bara är en punkt som inte har något begrepp om rotation."

#: ../../manual/editors/3dview/controls/pivot_point/active_element.rst:48
msgid "Left column: starting situation, right column: after rotation."
msgstr "Vänster kolumn: utgångsläge, höger kolumn: efter rotation."

#: ../../manual/editors/3dview/controls/pivot_point/bounding_box_center.rst:4
#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/introduction.rst:363
msgid "Bounding Box Center"
msgstr "Begränsande box Centrum"

#: ../../manual/editors/3dview/controls/pivot_point/bounding_box_center.rst:9
msgid ":menuselection:`Header --> Transform Pivot Point --> Bounding Box Center` (:bl-icon:`pivot_boundbox`)"
msgstr ":menuselection:`Huvud --> Transform Pivot Point --> Bounding Box Center` (:bl-icon:`pivot_boundbox`)"

#: ../../manual/editors/3dview/controls/pivot_point/bounding_box_center.rst:12
msgid "In this mode, the pivot point lies at the center of the bounding box, which is a box that's wrapped as tightly as possible around the selection while still being aligned to the world axes."
msgstr "I det här läget ligger pivotpunkten i mitten av bounding box, som är en box som är lindad så tätt som möjligt runt markeringen samtidigt som den fortfarande är i linje med världsaxlarna."

#: ../../manual/editors/3dview/controls/pivot_point/bounding_box_center.rst:19
msgid "The pivot point becomes the center of the bounding box *around the selected objects' origin points*, not their geometry."
msgstr "Pivotpunkten blir centrum för begränsningsrutan * runt de valda objektens ursprungspunkter*, inte deras geometri."

#: ../../manual/editors/3dview/controls/pivot_point/bounding_box_center.rst:22
msgid "This means that, if you have a single object selected, the pivot point is the same as the object's :doc:`origin point </scene_layout/object/origin>` -- which can be customized and doesn't have to be in the center. In the example below, the orange rectangle has it in a corner instead."
msgstr "Det innebär att om du har ett enda objekt markerat är pivotpunkten densamma som objektets :doc:`origin point </scene_layout/object/origin>` - som kan anpassas och inte behöver vara i mitten. I exemplet nedan har den orangefärgade rektangeln den i ett hörn istället."

#: ../../manual/editors/3dview/controls/pivot_point/bounding_box_center.rst:30
msgid "Single object rotation."
msgstr "Rotation av ett enda objekt."

#: ../../manual/editors/3dview/controls/pivot_point/bounding_box_center.rst:32
msgid "If you have multiple objects selected, the pivot point becomes the center of an imaginary box around their origins."
msgstr "Om du har flera objekt markerade blir pivotpunkten centrum för en imaginär box runt deras ursprung."

#: ../../manual/editors/3dview/controls/pivot_point/bounding_box_center.rst:35
msgid "The image below shows the difference between Bounding Box Center and :doc:`/editors/3dview/controls/pivot_point/median_point`. The latter calculates the average position of the origins, meaning that the pivot point shifts towards the area with the most objects."
msgstr "Bilden nedan visar skillnaden mellan Bounding Box Center och :doc:`/editors/3dview/controls/pivot_point/median_point`. Den senare beräknar den genomsnittliga positionen för ursprunget, vilket innebär att pivotpunkten flyttas mot det område som har flest objekt."

#: ../../manual/editors/3dview/controls/pivot_point/bounding_box_center.rst:43
#: ../../manual/editors/3dview/controls/pivot_point/bounding_box_center.rst:62
msgid "Difference between \"Bounding Box Center\" (left) and \"Median Point\" (right)."
msgstr "Skillnad mellan \"Bounding Box Center\" (vänster) och \"Median Point\" (höger)."

#: ../../manual/editors/3dview/controls/pivot_point/bounding_box_center.rst:49
msgid "The pivot point becomes the center of the bounding box around the selected mesh elements."
msgstr "Pivotpunkten blir centrum för den begränsande boxen runt de valda mesh-elementen."

#: ../../manual/editors/3dview/controls/pivot_point/bounding_box_center.rst:54
msgid "The effects of rotation in different mesh selection modes. The pivot point is shown by a yellow circle."
msgstr "Effekterna av rotation i olika lägen för val av nät. Svängpunkten visas med en gul cirkel."

#: ../../manual/editors/3dview/controls/pivot_point/bounding_box_center.rst:57
msgid "Median Point may again give a different result."
msgstr "Median Point kan återigen ge ett annat resultat."

#: ../../manual/editors/3dview/controls/pivot_point/index.rst:6
msgid "Transform Pivot Point"
msgstr "Transformera Pivot Point"

#: ../../manual/editors/3dview/controls/pivot_point/index.rst:11
msgid ":menuselection:`Header --> Transform Pivot Point`"
msgstr ":menuselection:`Huvud --> Transform Pivot Point`"

#: ../../manual/editors/3dview/controls/pivot_point/index.rst:14
msgid "The *Pivot Point* determines the location of the :doc:`Object Gizmo </editors/3dview/display/gizmo>`. Changing this location can make it easier to perform transformations around the point you want."
msgstr "*Pivot Point* bestämmer platsen för :doc:`Objektet Gizmo </editors/3dview/display/gizmo>`. Om du ändrar denna plats kan det bli lättare att utföra transformationer runt den punkt du vill ha."

#: ../../manual/editors/3dview/controls/pivot_point/index.rst:22
msgid "With the default \"Median Point\" pivot point (left) it's tricky to bring the second wheel spoke into place, but with \"3D Cursor\" (right) it's easy."
msgstr "Med den förinställda pivotpunkten \"Median Point\" (vänster) är det svårt att få den andra hjuleken på plats, men med \"3D Cursor\" (höger) är det enkelt."

#: ../../manual/editors/3dview/controls/pivot_point/index.rst:27
msgid "The Pivot Point can be changed using a selector in the 3D Viewport's header:"
msgstr "Pivotpunkten kan ändras med hjälp av en väljare i 3D-visningens huvud:"

#: ../../manual/editors/3dview/controls/pivot_point/index.rst:33
msgid "Pivot Types"
msgstr "Pivottyper"

#: ../../manual/editors/3dview/controls/pivot_point/individual_origins.rst:4
msgid "Individual Origins"
msgstr "Individuellt ursprung"

#: ../../manual/editors/3dview/controls/pivot_point/individual_origins.rst:9
msgid ":menuselection:`Header --> Transform Pivot Point --> Individual Origins` (:bl-icon:`pivot_individual`)"
msgstr ":menuselection:`Huvud --> Transform Pivot Point --> Individuella ursprung` (:bl-icon:`pivot_individual`)"

#: ../../manual/editors/3dview/controls/pivot_point/individual_origins.rst:12
msgid "While the other pivot point modes transform the whole selection around one point, Individual Origins transforms each item around itself."
msgstr "Medan de andra pivotpoint-lägena transformerar hela urvalet runt en punkt, transformerar Individual Origins varje objekt runt sig självt."

#: ../../manual/editors/3dview/controls/pivot_point/individual_origins.rst:18
msgid "Each object gets transformed around its :doc:`origin </scene_layout/object/origin>`, which is a point that can be chosen freely and doesn't have to be in the center. In the example below, the orange rectangle has it in a corner instead."
msgstr "Varje objekt transformeras runt sitt :doc:`ursprung </scene_layout/object/origin>`, vilket är en punkt som kan väljas fritt och inte behöver vara i mitten. I exemplet nedan har den orangefärgade rektangeln den i ett hörn istället."

#: ../../manual/editors/3dview/controls/pivot_point/individual_origins.rst:25
msgid "Rotation around individual origins."
msgstr "Rotation runt individuella ursprung."

#: ../../manual/editors/3dview/controls/pivot_point/individual_origins.rst:27
msgid "The images below compare Individual Origins to :doc:`/editors/3dview/controls/pivot_point/median_point`."
msgstr "Bilderna nedan jämför Individual Origins med :doc:`/editors/3dview/controls/pivot_point/median_point`."

#: ../../manual/editors/3dview/controls/pivot_point/individual_origins.rst:33
#: ../../manual/editors/3dview/controls/pivot_point/individual_origins.rst:49
msgid "Starting situation, rotation around Individual Origins, rotation around Median Point."
msgstr "Utgångsläge, rotation kring individuellt ursprung, rotation kring medelpunkt."

#: ../../manual/editors/3dview/controls/pivot_point/individual_origins.rst:38
#: ../../manual/editors/3dview/controls/pivot_point/individual_origins.rst:54
msgid "Starting situation, scaling using Individual Origins, scaling using Median Point."
msgstr "Utgångsläge, skalning med hjälp av Individual Origins, skalning med hjälp av Median Point."

#: ../../manual/editors/3dview/controls/pivot_point/individual_origins.rst:44
msgid "Each selected element is transformed around its own centerpoint."
msgstr "Varje valt element transformeras runt sin egen mittpunkt."

#: ../../manual/editors/3dview/controls/pivot_point/individual_origins.rst:56
msgid "When you transform adjacent faces or edges, they are treated as a single element (meaning they don't become disconnected)."
msgstr "När du transformerar angränsande ytor eller kanter behandlas de som ett enda element (vilket innebär att de inte blir bortkopplade)."

#: ../../manual/editors/3dview/controls/pivot_point/median_point.rst:4
msgid "Median Point"
msgstr "Medianpunkt"

#: ../../manual/editors/3dview/controls/pivot_point/median_point.rst:9
msgid ":menuselection:`Header --> Transform Pivot Point --> Median Point` (:bl-icon:`pivot_median`)"
msgstr ":menuselection:`Huvud --> Transform Pivot Point --> Median Point` (:bl-icon:`pivot_median`)"

#: ../../manual/editors/3dview/controls/pivot_point/median_point.rst:12
msgid "Places the pivot point at the averaged-out position of the selected items."
msgstr "Placerar pivotpunkten vid den genomsnittliga positionen för de valda objekten."

#: ../../manual/editors/3dview/controls/pivot_point/median_point.rst:18
msgid "In Object Mode, the Median Point is the averaged-out position of the :doc:`origins </scene_layout/object/origin>` of the selected objects. The shape and size of the objects is not taken into account."
msgstr "I Object Mode är Median Point den genomsnittliga positionen för :doc:`origins </scene_layout/object/origin>` för de valda objekten. Objektens form och storlek tas inte med i beräkningen."

#: ../../manual/editors/3dview/controls/pivot_point/median_point.rst:22
msgid "Origins can be chosen freely and can even lie outside their object's geometry, so that the Median Point is not always what you might expect."
msgstr "Ursprung kan väljas fritt och kan till och med ligga utanför objektets geometri, så att medianpunkten inte alltid är vad du kan förvänta dig."

#: ../../manual/editors/3dview/controls/pivot_point/median_point.rst:30
msgid "Median points in Object Mode."
msgstr "Medianpunkter i Object Mode."

#: ../../manual/editors/3dview/controls/pivot_point/median_point.rst:36
msgid "In Edit Mode, the Median Point is the averaged-out position of the selected vertices. This means that the pivot point will shift towards the area with the densest geometry."
msgstr "I Redigera Mode är Median Point den genomsnittliga positionen för de valda topparna. Detta innebär att pivotpunkten flyttas mot det område som har den tätaste geometrin."

#: ../../manual/editors/3dview/controls/pivot_point/median_point.rst:40
msgid "In the example below, the pivot point lies perfectly in the middle if both cubes have the same number of vertices, but heavily leans towards the side if one cube is subdivided -- even though both cubes still have the same size."
msgstr "I exemplet nedan ligger pivotpunkten perfekt i mitten om båda kuberna har samma antal hörn, men lutar kraftigt åt sidan om den ena kuben delas upp - trots att båda kuberna fortfarande har samma storlek."

#: ../../manual/editors/3dview/controls/pivot_point/median_point.rst:50
msgid "Median points in Edit Mode."
msgstr "Medianpunkter i redigeringsläget."

#: ../../manual/editors/3dview/controls/proportional_editing.rst:6
#: ../../manual/editors/dope_sheet/editing.rst:147
#: ../../manual/modeling/meshes/editing/face/extrude_faces.rst:70
#: ../../manual/modeling/meshes/editing/face/extrude_faces_normal.rst:29
#: ../../manual/modeling/meshes/editing/mesh/transform/shear.rst:39
#: ../../manual/modeling/meshes/uv/editing.rst:645
#: ../../manual/scene_layout/object/editing/transform/move.rst:47
#: ../../manual/scene_layout/object/editing/transform/rotate.rst:43
#: ../../manual/scene_layout/object/editing/transform/scale.rst:48
#: ../../manual/scene_layout/object/tools/scale_cage.rst:43
msgid "Proportional Editing"
msgstr "Proportionell redigering"

#: ../../manual/editors/3dview/controls/proportional_editing.rst:10
#: ../../manual/modeling/meshes/editing/mesh/transform/shear.rst:10
#: ../../manual/modeling/metas/properties.rst:16
msgid "Object and Edit Mode"
msgstr "Objekt- och redigeringsläge"

#: ../../manual/editors/3dview/controls/proportional_editing.rst:11
msgid ":menuselection:`Header --> Proportional Editing`"
msgstr ":menuselection:`Huvud --> Proportionell redigering`"

#: ../../manual/editors/3dview/controls/proportional_editing.rst:18
msgid "Proportional Editing popover."
msgstr "Popover för proportionell redigering."

#: ../../manual/editors/3dview/controls/proportional_editing.rst:20
msgid "Proportional Editing is a way of transforming selected elements while also affecting the nearby unselected elements. The farther away an unselected element is, the less it will be affected (hence the \"proportional\"). This feature is very useful for smoothly deforming dense meshes."
msgstr "Proportionell redigering är ett sätt att förändra valda element samtidigt som man påverkar närliggande omarkerade element. Ju längre bort ett omarkerat element befinner sig, desto mindre påverkas det (därav \"proportionell\"). Denna funktion är mycket användbar för smidig deformering av täta maskor."

#: ../../manual/editors/3dview/controls/proportional_editing.rst:26
msgid "Blender also has a :ref:`painting-sculpting-index` workflow that contains brushes and tools for proportionally editing a mesh without seeing the individual vertices."
msgstr "Blender har också ett :ref:`painting-sculpting-index`-arbetsflöde som innehåller penslar och verktyg för proportionell redigering av ett mesh utan att se de enskilda vertikalerna."

#: ../../manual/editors/3dview/controls/proportional_editing.rst:33
msgid "Disable :kbd:`O`"
msgstr "Inaktivera :kbd:`O`"

#: ../../manual/editors/3dview/controls/proportional_editing.rst:34
msgid "Proportional Editing is off, only selected vertices will be affected."
msgstr "Om Proportional Redigeraing är avstängd påverkas endast markerade hörnpunkter."

#: ../../manual/editors/3dview/controls/proportional_editing.rst:35
msgid "Enable :kbd:`O`"
msgstr "Aktivera :kbd:`O`"

#: ../../manual/editors/3dview/controls/proportional_editing.rst:36
msgid "Vertices other than the selected vertex are affected, within a defined radius."
msgstr "Andra vertex än den markerade påverkas inom en definierad radie."

#: ../../manual/editors/3dview/controls/proportional_editing.rst:42
msgid "Proportional Size"
msgstr "Proportionell storlek"

#: ../../manual/editors/3dview/controls/proportional_editing.rst:44
msgid "You can increase or decrease the radius of the tool's influence during a transform operation from the Proportional Editing popover or with :kbd:`WheelUp`/:kbd:`WheelDown`, or :kbd:`PageUp`/:kbd:`PageDown` respectively. As you change the radius, the points surrounding your selection will adjust their positions accordingly."
msgstr "Du kan öka eller minska verktygets influensradie under en transformationsoperation från popup-rutan Proportional Redigeraing eller med :kbd:`WheelUp`/:kbd:`WheelDown` respektive :kbd:`PageUp`/:kbd:`PageDown`. När du ändrar radien kommer de punkter som omger ditt val att justera sina positioner i enlighet med detta."

#: ../../manual/editors/3dview/controls/proportional_editing.rst:52
msgid "Influence circle."
msgstr "Influenscirkel."

#: ../../manual/editors/3dview/controls/proportional_editing.rst:60
msgid "While editing, you can change the curve profile by either clicking the *Falloff* icon in the header or pressing :kbd:`Shift-O` to get a pie menu."
msgstr "När du redigerar kan du ändra kurvprofilen genom att antingen klicka på *Falloff*-ikonen i sidhuvudet eller trycka på :kbd:`Shift-O` för att få fram en cirkelmeny."

#: ../../manual/editors/3dview/controls/proportional_editing.rst:67
msgid "Constant, No Falloff."
msgstr "Konstant, ingen avklingning."

#: ../../manual/editors/3dview/controls/proportional_editing.rst:71
msgid "Random Falloff."
msgstr "Slumpmässigt bortfall."

#: ../../manual/editors/3dview/controls/proportional_editing.rst:75
msgid "Linear Falloff."
msgstr "Linjär falloff."

#: ../../manual/editors/3dview/controls/proportional_editing.rst:79
msgid "Sharp Falloff."
msgstr "Sharp Falloff."

#: ../../manual/editors/3dview/controls/proportional_editing.rst:83
msgid "Root Falloff."
msgstr "Root Falloff."

#: ../../manual/editors/3dview/controls/proportional_editing.rst:87
msgid "Sphere Falloff."
msgstr "Sfär Falloff."

#: ../../manual/editors/3dview/controls/proportional_editing.rst:91
msgid "Smooth Falloff."
msgstr "Smidig falloff."

#: ../../manual/editors/3dview/controls/proportional_editing.rst:95
msgid "Inverse Square Falloff."
msgstr "Inverse Square Falloff."

#: ../../manual/editors/3dview/controls/proportional_editing.rst:103
msgid "Proportional Editing is typically used in *Edit Mode*, but it can also be used in *Object Mode*. The tool then works on entire objects rather than individual mesh components."
msgstr "Proportional Redigeraing används vanligtvis i *Redigera Mode*, men det kan också användas i *Object Mode*. Verktyget arbetar då på hela objekt i stället för på enskilda mesh-komponenter."

#: ../../manual/editors/3dview/controls/proportional_editing.rst:106
msgid "In the image below, the leftmost cylinder is being scaled up vertically, which also affects the cylinders near it."
msgstr "I bilden nedan skalas den längst till vänster stående cylindern upp vertikalt, vilket även påverkar cylindrarna i närheten."

#: ../../manual/editors/3dview/controls/proportional_editing.rst:113
msgid "Proportional Editing in Object Mode."
msgstr "Proportionell redigering i objektläge."

#: ../../manual/editors/3dview/controls/proportional_editing.rst:119
msgid "When working with dense geometry, it can become difficult to make subtle adjustments without causing visible lumps and creases in the model's surface. When you face situations like this, Proportional Editing can help."
msgstr "När man arbetar med tät geometri kan det bli svårt att göra subtila justeringar utan att orsaka synliga klumpar och veck i modellens yta. När du ställs inför sådana situationer kan Proportional Redigeraing hjälpa dig."

#: ../../manual/editors/3dview/controls/proportional_editing.rst:126
msgid "Proportional Editing in Edit Mode."
msgstr "Proportionell redigering i redigeringsläget."

#: ../../manual/editors/3dview/controls/proportional_editing.rst:134
msgid "Connected Only :kbd:`Alt-O`"
msgstr "Endast anslutna :kbd:`Alt-O`"

#: ../../manual/editors/3dview/controls/proportional_editing.rst:135
msgid "Rather than using a radius only, the proportional falloff spreads via connected geometry. This means that you can proportionally edit the vertices in a finger of a hand without affecting the other fingers. While the other vertices are physically close (in 3D space), they are far away following the topological edge connections of the mesh. The icon will have a blue center when *Connected* is active. This mode is only available in *Edit Mode*."
msgstr "I stället för att bara använda en radie sprider sig den proportionella avsmalningen via ansluten geometri. Det innebär att du kan proportionellt redigera vertikalerna i ett finger på en hand utan att påverka de andra fingrarna. Även om de andra hörnen är fysiskt nära (i 3D-rymden) är de långt borta enligt de topologiska kantkopplingarna i nätet. Ikonen har en blå mitt när *Connected* är aktiv. Detta läge är endast tillgängligt i *Redigera Mode*."

#: ../../manual/editors/3dview/controls/proportional_editing.rst:144
msgid "Projected from View"
msgstr "Projiceras från View"

#: ../../manual/editors/3dview/controls/proportional_editing.rst:145
msgid "Depth along the view is ignored when applying the radius."
msgstr "Djupet längs vyn ignoreras när radien tillämpas."

#: ../../manual/editors/3dview/controls/proportional_editing.rst:149
msgid "The difference between having \"Projected from View\" disabled (left) and enabled (right)."
msgstr "Skillnaden mellan att ha \"Projected from View\" avaktiverat (vänster) och aktiverat (höger)."

#: ../../manual/editors/3dview/controls/proportional_editing.rst:155
msgid "The image below shows the final render of a low-poly landscape obtained by moving up the vertices of a triangulated grid with *Proportional Editing* enabled."
msgstr "Bilden nedan visar den slutliga renderingen av ett low-poly-landskap som erhållits genom att flytta upp topparna i ett triangulerat rutnät med *Proportional Redigeraing* aktiverat."

#: ../../manual/editors/3dview/controls/proportional_editing.rst:161
msgid "A landscape obtained via Proportional Editing."
msgstr "Ett landskap som erhållits via Proportional Redigeraing."

#: ../../manual/editors/3dview/controls/snapping.rst:10
msgid ":menuselection:`Header --> Snapping`"
msgstr ":menuselection:`Huvud --> Snapping`"

#: ../../manual/editors/3dview/controls/snapping.rst:11
#: ../../manual/editors/nla/editing/strip.rst:346
#: ../../manual/interface/keymap/industry_compatible.rst:28
msgid ":kbd:`Shift-Tab`"
msgstr ":kbd:`Shift-Tab`"

#: ../../manual/editors/3dview/controls/snapping.rst:16
msgid "Snap menu."
msgstr "Snap meny."

#: ../../manual/editors/3dview/controls/snapping.rst:18
msgid "Snapping lets you easily align objects and mesh elements to others. It can be toggled by clicking :bl-icon:`snap_off` (Snap Off) / :bl-icon:`snap_on` (Snap On) in the 3D Viewport's header, or more temporarily by holding :kbd:`Ctrl`."
msgstr "Med Snapping kan du enkelt rikta in objekt och mesh-element mot andra. Det kan växlas genom att klicka på :bl-icon:`snap_off` (Snap Off) / :bl-icon:`snap_on` (Snap On) i 3D-visningens huvud, eller mer tillfälligt genom att hålla in :kbd:`Ctrl`."

#: ../../manual/editors/3dview/controls/snapping.rst:28
msgid ":doc:`Transform Modal Map </modeling/transform/modal_map>` for further keyboard shortcuts."
msgstr ":doc:`Transform Modal Map </modeling/transform/modal_map>` för ytterligare kortkommandon."

