#: ../../manual/modeling/curves/structure.rst:51
#: ../../manual/modeling/curves/tools/draw.rst:0
#: ../../manual/modeling/curves_new/editing/curves.rst:0
#: ../../manual/modeling/curves_new/structure.rst:49
#: ../../manual/modeling/curves_new/tools/draw.rst:0
#: ../../manual/modeling/geometry_nodes/curve/operations/fillet_curve.rst:0
#: ../../manual/modeling/geometry_nodes/curve/write/set_spline_type.rst:0
msgid "Bézier"
msgstr "Banan ritad med Form: Triangel in i Bézier-läge, med en utjämning på 40"

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/fcurves/properties.rst:135
msgid "Bézier."
msgstr "Bézier."

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/fcurves/properties.rst:137
msgid "The default interpolation, which is smooth in both values and speed."
msgstr "Standardinterpolering, som är jämn i både värden och hastighet."

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/fcurves/properties.rst:141
msgid "F-Curves for properties that only accept discrete values will always have a stair step pattern, no matter which option you chose."
msgstr "F-kurvor för egenskaper som endast accepterar diskreta värden kommer alltid att ha ett trappstegsmönster, oavsett vilket alternativ du väljer."

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/fcurves/properties.rst:0
msgid "Easing (by strength)"
msgstr "Lättnader (efter styrka)"

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/fcurves/properties.rst:147
msgid "A set of interpolations that specialize in accelerating or decelerating an value, \"easing\" it from a stationary into a moving state or vice versa."
msgstr "En uppsättning interpolationer som är specialiserade på att accelerera eller decelerera ett värde, \"underlätta\" det från ett stationärt till ett rörligt tillstånd eller vice versa."

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/fcurves/properties.rst:152
msgid "For more info and a few live demos, see `easings.net <https://easings.net>`__ and `Robert Penner's Easing Functions <http://robertpenner.com/easing>`__."
msgstr "För mer information och några live-demonstrationer, se `easings.net <https://easings.net>`__ och `Robert Penner's Easing Functions <http://robertpenner.com/easing>`__."

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/fcurves/properties.rst:0
msgid "Dynamic Effects"
msgstr "Dynamiska effekter"

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/fcurves/properties.rst:159
msgid "These additional easing types imitate (fake) physics-based effects like bouncing."
msgstr "Dessa extra lättnadstyper imiterar (falska) fysikbaserade effekter som studsning."

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/fcurves/properties.rst:162
msgid "With *Ease In*, the value first moves away from the target and then shoots towards it. With *Ease Out*, it goes towards the target, overshoots it, and then returns."
msgstr "Med *Ease In* rör sig värdet först bort från målet och skjuter sedan mot det. Med *Ease Out* går det mot målet, skjuter över det och återvänder sedan."

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/fcurves/properties.rst:166
msgid "The size and direction (i.e. above/below the curve) of the overshoot."
msgstr "Storlek och riktning (dvs. över/under kurvan) på överskridandet."

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/fcurves/properties.rst:168
msgid "Bounce"
msgstr "Studsa"

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/fcurves/properties.rst:169
msgid "Makes the value bounce a few times with exponential decay, like a tennis ball that was dropped on the floor."
msgstr "Får värdet att studsa några gånger med exponentiell avklingning, som en tennisboll som tappats på golvet."

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/fcurves/properties.rst:172
#: ../../manual/glossary/index.rst:343
#: ../../manual/sculpt_paint/sculpting/brushes/snake_hook.rst:0
#: ../../manual/sculpt_paint/sculpting/tools/transforms.rst:0
msgid "Elastic"
msgstr "Elastisk"

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/fcurves/properties.rst:173
msgid "Makes the value overshoot the target, then rebound and undershoot it, then overshoot it again... with ever-decreasing intensity until it eventually settles."
msgstr "Det får värdet att överskrida målet, sedan studsa tillbaka och underskrida det, sedan överskrida det igen ... med ständigt minskande intensitet tills det så småningom sätter sig."

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/fcurves/properties.rst:177
msgid "How far the value initially overshoots its target."
msgstr "Hur mycket värdet initialt överskrider sitt mål."

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/fcurves/properties.rst:178
#: ../../manual/grease_pencil/visual_effects/shadow.rst:60
#: ../../manual/grease_pencil/visual_effects/wave_distortion.rst:25
#: ../../manual/render/freestyle/view_layer/line_style/modifiers/color/noise.rst:15
#: ../../manual/render/freestyle/view_layer/line_style/modifiers/color/noise.rst:11
msgid "Period"
msgstr "Period"

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/fcurves/properties.rst:179
msgid "How much time there is between each oscillation."
msgstr "Hur lång tid det är mellan varje svängning."

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/fcurves/properties.rst:184
msgid "This option only applies to the *Easing* and *Dynamic Effects* categories above."
msgstr "Detta alternativ gäller endast för kategorierna *Easing* och *Dynamic Effects* ovan."

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/fcurves/properties.rst:186
msgid "Automatic Easing"
msgstr "Automatisk lättnad"

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/fcurves/properties.rst:187
msgid "Automatically pick the most commonly used type: *Ease In* when using one of the *Easing* interpolations, and *Ease Out* when using one of the *Dynamic Effects*."
msgstr "Välj automatiskt den mest använda typen: *Ease In* när du använder någon av interpoleringarna *Easing* och *Ease Out* när du använder någon av de *Dynamiska effekterna*."

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/fcurves/properties.rst:189
msgid "Ease In"
msgstr "Lätt att komma in"

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/fcurves/properties.rst:190
msgid "The value accelerates, moving slowly at the beginning of the curve segment and speeding up towards the end."
msgstr "Värdet accelererar, rör sig långsamt i början av kurvsegmentet och ökar hastigheten mot slutet."

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/fcurves/properties.rst:191
msgid "Ease Out"
msgstr "Lättare att komma ut"

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/fcurves/properties.rst:192
msgid "The value decelerates, moving quickly at the beginning of the curve segment and slowing down towards the end."
msgstr "Värdet avtar, rör sig snabbt i början av kurvsegmentet och saktar in mot slutet."

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/fcurves/properties.rst:193
msgid "Ease In Out"
msgstr "Enkelhet In Ut"

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/fcurves/properties.rst:194
msgid "The value moves slowly in the beginning, speeds up towards the middle, and slows down again towards the end."
msgstr "Värdet rör sig långsamt i början, ökar hastigheten mot mitten och saktar ner igen mot slutet."

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/fcurves/properties.rst:198
msgid "Key Frame"
msgstr "Nyckelram"

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/fcurves/properties.rst:199
msgid "The frame of the active keyframe."
msgstr "Den aktiva nyckelramens bildruta."

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/fcurves/properties.rst:201
msgid "The value of the active keyframe."
msgstr "Värdet för den aktiva nyckelrutan."

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/fcurves/properties.rst:207
msgid "Left/Right Handle Type"
msgstr "Handtagstyp vänster/höger"

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/fcurves/properties.rst:208
msgid "When the keyframe's interpolation is set to *Bézier*, the shape of the curve around it is influenced by its handles. Each handle has its own type which determines if (and how) Blender positions it automatically, and if not, how much freedom you have in positioning it manually."
msgstr "När nyckelramens interpolering är inställd på *Bézier* påverkas formen på kurvan runt den av dess handtag. Varje handtag har sin egen typ som avgör om (och hur) Blender positionerar det automatiskt, och om inte, hur mycket frihet du har att positionera det manuellt."

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/fcurves/properties.rst:212
msgid "You can change the handles' types in multiple ways: using these dropdowns in the Sidebar; through the menu :menuselection:`Key --> Handle Type`; or by pressing :kbd:`V` and selecting from the popup menu."
msgstr "Du kan ändra handtagens typ på flera sätt: med hjälp av rullgardinsmenyerna i sidofältet, via menyn :menuselection:`Key --> Handle Type` eller genom att trycka på :kbd:`V` och välja från popup-menyn."

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/fcurves/properties.rst:215
msgid "If you want to change an automatic handle's position, just drag it; you don't need to manually change its type first."
msgstr "Om du vill ändra positionen för ett automatiskt handtag är det bara att dra i det, du behöver inte ändra typen manuellt först."

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/fcurves/properties.rst:223
msgid "Auto handles."
msgstr "Auto handtag."

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/fcurves/properties.rst:225
msgid "Automatic handles that produce smooth curves."
msgstr "Automatiska handtag som ger mjuka kurvor."

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/fcurves/properties.rst:0
msgid "Auto Clamped"
msgstr "Automatisk fastspänning"

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/fcurves/properties.rst:232
msgid "Auto clamped handles."
msgstr "Automatiskt fastspända handtag."

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/fcurves/properties.rst:234
msgid "Automatic handles clamped to prevent overshoots and changes in the curve direction between keyframes (S-shapes)."
msgstr "Automatiska handtag kläms fast för att förhindra överskridanden och ändringar i kurvans riktning mellan keyframes (S-former)."

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/fcurves/properties.rst:242
msgid "Vector handles."
msgstr "Vektorhandtag."

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/fcurves/properties.rst:244
msgid "Automatic handles that produce straight curve segments (like linear interpolation)."
msgstr "Automatiska handtag som producerar raka kurvsegment (som linjär interpolering)."

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/fcurves/properties.rst:251
msgid "Aligned handles."
msgstr "Justerade handtag."

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/fcurves/properties.rst:253
msgid "Manual handles, which are however locked together to always point in opposite directions. This results in a curve that is always smooth at the control point."
msgstr "Manuella handtag, som dock låses ihop så att de alltid pekar i motsatt riktning. Detta resulterar i en kurva som alltid är jämn vid kontrollpunkten."

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/fcurves/properties.rst:261
msgid "Free handles."
msgstr "Fria handtag."

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/fcurves/properties.rst:263
msgid "Manual handles that can be moved independently, and thus can result in a sharp change of direction."
msgstr "Manuella handtag som kan flyttas oberoende av varandra och därmed kan ge en kraftig riktningsförändring."

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/fcurves/properties.rst:269
msgid "Frame, Value"
msgstr "Ram, värde"

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/fcurves/properties.rst:270
msgid "The frame and value for the left/right handle of the active keyframe."
msgstr "Ram och värde för vänster/höger handtag för den aktiva keyframen."

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/index.rst:6
msgid "Graph Editor"
msgstr "Graph Redigerare"

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/introduction.rst:7
msgid "The Graph Editor lets you edit animation curves, which determine how properties change over time."
msgstr "Med Graph Redigerare kan du redigera animationskurvor, som bestämmer hur egenskaper förändras över tid."

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/introduction.rst:11
msgid "The Graph Editor."
msgstr "Graf-editorn."

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/introduction.rst:17
msgid "The curve view allows you to view and edit :doc:`F-Curves </editors/graph_editor/fcurves/introduction>`. An F-Curve has several key parts:"
msgstr "Med kurvvyn kan du visa och redigera :doc:`F-kurvor </editors/graph_editor/fcurves/introduction>`. En F-kurva har flera viktiga delar:"

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/introduction.rst:21
msgid "The curve describes how the value of a property (Y axis) evolves over time (X axis)."
msgstr "Kurvan beskriver hur värdet på en egenskap (Y-axeln) utvecklas över tiden (X-axeln)."

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/introduction.rst:22
msgid ":doc:`Keyframes </animation/keyframes/index>`"
msgstr ":doc:`Keyframes </animation/keyframes/index>`"

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/introduction.rst:23
msgid "Keyframes are user-defined values on certain frames and are represented by little black discs that become orange when selected. The values on the other frames are calculated automatically by interpolating between these keyframes."
msgstr "Keyframes är användardefinierade värden på vissa bildrutor och representeras av små svarta skivor som blir orange när de väljs. Värdena på de andra bildrutorna beräknas automatiskt genom interpolering mellan dessa keyframes."

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/introduction.rst:27
msgid ":ref:`Handles <editors-graph-fcurves-settings-handles>`"
msgstr ":ref:`Handtag <editors-graph-fcurves-settings-handles>`"

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/introduction.rst:28
msgid "Each keyframe has two handles -- points that can be dragged around to influence the shape of the curve around it."
msgstr "Varje keyframe har två handtag - punkter som kan dras runt för att påverka formen på kurvan runt den."

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/introduction.rst:33
msgid "A simple curve. The discs are keyframes, and the circles are their handles."
msgstr "En enkel kurva. Skivorna är keyframes och cirklarna är deras handtag."

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/introduction.rst:37
msgid "See :doc:`F-Curves </editors/graph_editor/fcurves/introduction>` for more info."
msgstr "Se :doc:`F-Curves </editors/graph_editor/fcurves/introduction>` för mer information."

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/introduction.rst:46
msgid "Pan the view by dragging with :kbd:`MMB`."
msgstr "Panorera vyn genom att dra med :kbd:`MMB`."

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/introduction.rst:48
msgid "Zoom in and out with the mouse :kbd:`Wheel`."
msgstr "Zooma in och ut med musen :kbd:`Wheel`."

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/introduction.rst:49
msgid "Scale View"
msgstr "Skala vy"

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/introduction.rst:50
msgid "Scale the view horizontally or vertically by dragging with :kbd:`Ctrl-MMB`."
msgstr "Skala vyn horisontellt eller vertikalt genom att dra med :kbd:`Ctrl-MMB`."

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/introduction.rst:52
msgid "You can also use the scrollbars."
msgstr "Du kan också använda rullningslisterna."

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/introduction.rst:56
msgid "You can focus the view on the curve of an animated property by right clicking it and choosing :menuselection:`View in Graph Editor`. If you want to set up a hotkey for this, you need to open the :doc:`/editors/preferences/keymap` preferences, open the *User Interface* category, click *Add New*, fill in the operator name ``anim.view_curve_in_graph_editor``, and finally choose a shortcut. Normally this can be done more easily by right clicking the context menu item and choosing *Assign Shortcut*, but in this case, the shortcut would be added to the wrong category and not work."
msgstr "Du kan fokusera vyn på kurvan för en animerad egenskap genom att högerklicka på den och välja :menuselection:`View in Graph Redigerare`. Om du vill skapa en snabbtangent för detta måste du öppna inställningarna i :doc:`/editors/preferences/keymap`, öppna kategorin *User Interface*, klicka på *Add New*, fylla i operatörsnamnet `anim.view_curve_in_graph_editor` och slutligen välja en genväg. Normalt kan detta göras enklare genom att högerklicka på kontextmenyobjektet och välja *Assign Shortcut*, men i det här fallet skulle genvägen läggas till i fel kategori och inte fungera."

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/introduction.rst:69
msgid "Playhead & 2D Cursor"
msgstr "Playhead & 2D-markör"

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/introduction.rst:74
msgid "Graph Editor 2D Cursor."
msgstr "Graph Redigerare 2D-markör."

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/introduction.rst:76
msgid "The current frame is represented by a vertical blue line called the *Playhead*. As in the :doc:`Timeline </editors/timeline>`, you can move it by clicking or dragging with :kbd:`LMB` in the scrubbing area at the top."
msgstr "Den aktuella bildrutan representeras av en vertikal blå linje som kallas *Playhead*. Precis som i :doc:`Timeline </editors/timeline>` kan du flytta den genom att klicka eller dra med :kbd:`LMB` i skrubbområdet högst upp."

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/introduction.rst:80
msgid "Combined with the horizontal blue line, the Playhead forms the *2D Cursor* which can be used as a :doc:`pivot point </editors/3dview/controls/pivot_point/index>` for rotating and scaling. You can disable the horizontal line using :menuselection:`View --> Show Cursor` or :menuselection:`Sidebar --> View --> Show Cursor`."
msgstr "I kombination med den horisontella blå linjen bildar Playhead *2D Cursor* som kan användas som en :doc:`pivot point </editors/3dview/controls/pivot_point/index>` för rotation och skalning. Du kan inaktivera den horisontella linjen genom att använda :menuselection:`View --> Show Cursor` eller :menuselection:`Sidebar --> View --> Show Cursor`."

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/introduction.rst:85
msgid "The 2D Cursor can be moved by clicking or dragging with :kbd:`Shift-RMB` or by adjusting its coordinates in the :ref:`View tab <graph_editor-view-properties>` of the Sidebar."
msgstr "2D-markören kan flyttas genom att klicka eller dra med :kbd:`Shift-RMB` eller genom att justera dess koordinater i :ref:`View tab <graph_editor-view-properties>` i sidofältet."

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/introduction.rst:100
#: ../../manual/editors/image/navigating.rst:34
#: ../../manual/editors/nla/introduction.rst:49
#: ../../manual/editors/timeline.rst:269
#: ../../manual/editors/video_sequencer/sequencer/navigating.rst:29
msgid "Displays a pop-up panel to alter properties of the last completed operation. See :ref:`bpy.ops.screen.redo_last`."
msgstr "Visar en popup-panel för att ändra egenskaper för den senast slutförda operationen. Se :ref:`bpy.ops.screen.redo_last`."

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/introduction.rst:103
msgid "Shows or hides the :ref:`Channels Region <editors-graph_editor-channels_region>`."
msgstr "Visar eller döljer :ref:`Channels Region <editors-graph_editor-channels_region>`."

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/introduction.rst:115
msgid "Centers the area to the Playhead."
msgstr "Centrerar området till Playhead."

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/introduction.rst:135
msgid "Auto-Lock Key Axis"
msgstr "Auto-Lock Nyckelaxel"

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/introduction.rst:136
msgid "Automatically locks the movement of keyframes to the axis that best matches the direction of the mouse cursor."
msgstr "Låser automatiskt nyckelramarnas rörelse till den axel som bäst matchar muspekarens riktning."

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/introduction.rst:142
msgid "Shows the marker region. When disabled, the `Marker Menu`_ is also hidden and marker operators are not available in this editor."
msgstr "Visar markörområdet. När den är inaktiverad döljs även `Marker Menu`_ och marköroperatorer är inte tillgängliga i den här redigeraren."

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/introduction.rst:144
#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/introduction.rst:417
msgid "Show Cursor"
msgstr "Visa markör"

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/introduction.rst:145
msgid "Toggles the visibility of the horizontal blue line (see `Playhead & 2D Cursor`_)."
msgstr "Växlar synligheten för den horisontella blå linjen (se `Playhead & 2D Cursor`_)."

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/introduction.rst:147
msgid "Show timing in seconds instead of frames. As an example, the timestamp ``01:03+02`` means \"1 minute, 3 seconds, 2 frames.\""
msgstr "Visa tidsangivelser i sekunder istället för bildrutor. Som exempel betyder tidsstämpeln `01:03+02` \"1 minut, 3 sekunder, 2 bildrutor\""

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/introduction.rst:158
msgid "Show Extrapolation"
msgstr "Visa extrapolering"

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/introduction.rst:159
msgid "Toggles the visibility of the :ref:`extrapolated <editors-graph-fcurves-settings-extrapolation>` portion of curves."
msgstr "Växlar synligheten för :ref:`extrapolerad <editors-graph-fcurves-settings-extrapolation>`-delen av kurvorna."

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/introduction.rst:161
msgid "Show Handles :kbd:`Ctrl-H`"
msgstr "Visa handtag :kbd:`Ctrl-H`"

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/introduction.rst:162
msgid "Toggles the display of keyframe handles."
msgstr "Inaktiverar visning av keyframe-handtag."

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/introduction.rst:163
msgid "Only Selected Keyframes Handles"
msgstr "Endast valda nyckelramar Handtag"

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/introduction.rst:164
msgid "Only shows the handles for the selected keyframes."
msgstr "Visar endast handtagen för de markerade keyframes."

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/introduction.rst:186
msgid "Toggle Dope Sheet"
msgstr "Toggle Dope-ark"

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/introduction.rst:187
msgid "Changes the area's editor to the :doc:`Dope Sheet Editor </editors/dope_sheet/introduction>`."
msgstr "Ändrar områdets editor till :doc:`Dope Sheet Redigerare </editors/dope_sheet/introduction>`."

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/introduction.rst:202
msgid "Selects all keyframes and handles."
msgstr "Markerar alla nyckelramar och handtag."

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/introduction.rst:204
msgid "Clears the selection."
msgstr "Rensar markeringen."

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/introduction.rst:213
msgid "Lets you drag a box and selects the keyframes and handles inside it."
msgstr "Låter dig dra en ruta och väljer keyframes och handtag inuti den."

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/introduction.rst:215
msgid "Lets you drag a box and selects the keyframes and handles inside the corresponding time range, even if they're above or below the box."
msgstr "Låter dig dra en ruta och väljer keyframes och handtag inom motsvarande tidsintervall, även om de befinner sig ovanför eller under rutan."

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/introduction.rst:217
msgid "Box Select (Include Handles)"
msgstr "Box Välj (Inklusive handtag)"

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/introduction.rst:218
msgid "Selects keyframes and their handles inside the defined box."
msgstr "Väljer nyckelramar och deras handtag inom den definierade rutan."

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/introduction.rst:220
msgid "Displays a circle around the cursor, which you can drag over keyframes and handles to select them."
msgstr "Visar en cirkel runt markören, som du kan dra över keyframes och handtag för att markera dem."

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/introduction.rst:222
msgid "Lets you draw a freehand shape and selects the keyframes and handles inside it."
msgstr "Låter dig rita en form på fri hand och väljer keyframes och handtag inuti den."

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/introduction.rst:233
msgid "Selects keys that are on the same frame as a selected :doc:`marker </animation/markers>`."
msgstr "Väljer tangenter som befinner sig på samma ram som en vald :doc:`marker </animation/markers>`."

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/introduction.rst:252
msgid "Select Handles"
msgstr "Välj handtag"

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/introduction.rst:253
msgid "Selects the handles of the currently selected keyframes."
msgstr "Väljer handtagen för de aktuella keyframes som är markerade."

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/introduction.rst:254
msgid "Select Keys"
msgstr "Välj tangenter"

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/introduction.rst:255
msgid "Selects the keyframes of the currently selected handles."
msgstr "Väljer keyframes för de markerade handtagen."

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/introduction.rst:262
msgid "Select More :kbd:`Ctrl-NumpadPlus`"
msgstr "Välj mer :kbd:`Ctrl-NumpadPlus`"

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/introduction.rst:263
msgid "Expands the selection to include the neighbors (in time) of the currently selected keys."
msgstr "Utökar valet till att omfatta grannarna (i tid) till de aktuella valda tangenterna."

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/introduction.rst:264
msgid "Select Less :kbd:`Ctrl-NumpadMinus`"
msgstr "Välj mindre :kbd:`Ctrl-NumpadMinus`"

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/introduction.rst:265
msgid "Deselects keyframes with fewer than two selected neighbors."
msgstr "Avmarkerar keyframes med färre än två markerade grannar."

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/introduction.rst:272
msgid "Selects keys that are on the same curve as a key that's already selected."
msgstr "Väljer tangenter som ligger på samma kurva som en tangent som redan är vald."

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/introduction.rst:285
#: ../../manual/editors/nla/introduction.rst:152
#: ../../manual/editors/timeline.rst:346
msgid "For descriptions of the different marker tools, see :ref:`Editing Markers <animation-markers-editing>`."
msgstr "För beskrivningar av de olika markörverktygen, se :ref:`Redigering av markörer <animation-markers-editing>`."

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/introduction.rst:291
msgid "See :doc:`Editing Channels </editors/graph_editor/channels/editing>`."
msgstr "Se :doc:`Redigering av kanaler </editors/graph_editor/channels/editing>`."

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/introduction.rst:297
msgid "See :doc:`Editing F-Curves </editors/graph_editor/fcurves/editing>`."
msgstr "Se :doc:`Redigering av F-kurvor </editors/graph_editor/fcurves/editing>`."

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/introduction.rst:303
msgid "Scales the display of each curve so that they all (appear to) occupy the same value range, going from -1 to 1. This can make editing easier when you're working with curves whose value ranges are far apart."
msgstr "Skalar visningen av varje kurva så att de alla (verkar) ligga inom samma värdeintervall, från -1 till 1. Detta kan underlätta redigeringen när du arbetar med kurvor vars värdeintervall ligger långt ifrån varandra."

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/introduction.rst:307
msgid "When you enable this option, the view is zoomed accordingly and the area outside the normalized value range is darkened."
msgstr "När du aktiverar det här alternativet zoomas vyn i enlighet med detta och området utanför det normaliserade värdeområdet blir mörkare."

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/introduction.rst:310
msgid "If a preview range is defined, keyframes within the range are normalized, while the others are scaled proportionally."
msgstr "Om ett förhandsgranskningsområde definieras normaliseras keyframes inom området, medan de övriga skalas proportionellt."

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/introduction.rst:314
msgid "Auto Normalization"
msgstr "Automatisk normalisering"

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/introduction.rst:316
msgid "Automatically recalculate curve normalization on every curve edit."
msgstr "Beräkna automatiskt om kurvnormaliseringen vid varje kurvredigering."

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/introduction.rst:320
msgid "View Controls"
msgstr "Visa kontroller"

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/introduction.rst:324
msgid "View controls."
msgstr "Visa kontroller."

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/introduction.rst:326
msgid "Show Only Selected"
msgstr "Visa endast utvalda"

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/introduction.rst:327
msgid "Only show curves belonging to objects/bones/... that are selected."
msgstr "Visa endast kurvor som hör till objekt/ben/... som är markerade."

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/introduction.rst:330
msgid "Show Only Errors"
msgstr "Visa endast fel"

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/introduction.rst:333
msgid "Create Ghost Curves (framed F-Curve icon)"
msgstr "Skapa spökkurvor (inramad ikon för F-kurva)"

#: ../../manual/editors/graph_editor/introduction.rst:334
msgid "Creates a snapshot of the current curves and shows it in the background so that you can use it as a reference. Click the button again to clear the snapshot."
